ee\", \"Number of Connected Components in an Undirected Graph\", \"Redundant Connection\",\n301:                 \"Word Ladder\", \"Cheapest Flights Within K Stops\", \"Reconstruct Itinerary\", \"Network Delay Time\",\n302:                 \"Swim in Rising Water\", \"Alien Dictionary\", \"Min Cost to Connect All Points\", \"Critical Connections in a Network\"\n303:         };\n304: \n305:         String[] classicDpTitles = {\n306:                 \"Climbing Stairs\", \"Min Cost Climbing Stairs\", \"House Robber\", \"House Robber II\", \"Longest Palindromic Substring\",\n307:                 \"Palindromic Substrings\", \"Decode Ways\", \"Coin Change\", \"Maximum Product Subarray\", \"Word Break\",\n308:                 \"Longest Increasing Subsequence\", \"Partition Equal Subset Sum\", \"Unique Paths\", \"Longest Common Subsequence\",\n309:                 \"Best Time to Buy and Sell Stock with Cooldown\", \"Coin Change II\", \"Target Sum\", \"Interleaving String\",\n310:                 \"Edit Distance\", \"Burst Balloons\", \"Distinct Subsequences\", \"Regular Expression Matching\"\n311:         };\n312: \n313:         String[] classicTreeTitles = {\n314:                 \"Invert Binary Tree\", \"Maximum Depth of Binary Tree\", \"Diameter of Binary Tree\", \"Balanced Binary Tree\",\n315:                 \"Same Tree\", \"Subtree of Another Tree\", \"Lowest Common Ancestor of a BST\", \"Binary Tree Level Order Traversal\",\n316:                 \"Binary Tree Right Side View\", \"Count Good Nodes in Binary Tree\", \"Validate Binary Search Tree\",\n317:                 \"Kth Smallest Element in a BST\", \"Construct Binary Tree from Preorder and Inorder Traversal\",\n318:                 \"Binary Tree Maximum Path Sum\", \"Serialize and Deserialize Binary Tree\"\n319:         };\n320: \n321:         if (\"Arrays & Hashing\".equals(category) && index <= classicArrayTitles.length) {\n322:             return classicArrayTitles[index - 1];\n323:         } else if (\"Two Pointers & Sliding Window\".equals(category) && index <= classicTwoPointersTitles.length) {\n324:             return classicTwoPointersTitles[index - 1];\n325:         } else if (\"Binary Search\".equals(category) && index <= classicBinarySearchTitles.length) {\n326:             return classicBinarySearchTitles[index - 1];\n327:         } else if (\"Graphs\".equals(category) && index <= classicGraphTitles.length) {\n328:             return classicGraphTitles[index - 1];\n329:         } else if (\"Dynamic Programming\".equals(category) && index <= classicDpTitles.length) {\n330:             return classicDpTitles[index - 1];\n331:         } else if (\"Trees & BST\".equals(category) && index <= classicTreeTitles.length) {\n332:             return classicTreeTitles[index - 1];\n333:         }\n334: \n335:         // Programmatic naming with meaningful DSA patterns\n336:         String prefix = switch (category) {\n337:             case \"Arrays & Hashing\" -> \"Array & Hashing: \";\n338:             case \"Two Pointers & Sliding Window\" -> \"Window & Pointers: \";\n339:             case \"Binary Search\" -> \"Binary Search: \";\n340:             case \"Strings\" -> \"String Matrix: \";\n341:             case \"Linked List\" -> \"List Manipulation: \";\n342:             case \"Stack & Monotonic Stack\" -> \"Monotonic Stack: \";\n343:             case \"Queue & Deque\" -> \"Queue Stream: \";\n344:             case \"Trees & BST\" -> \"Tree Traversal: \";\n345:             case \"Heap / Priority Queue\" -> \"Priority Heap: \";\n346:             case \"Greedy\" -> \"Optimal Greedy: \";\n347:             case \"Backtracking\" -> \"State Backtracking: \";\n348:             case \"Graphs\" -> \"Graph Network: \";\n349:             case \"Dynamic Programming\" -> \"DP Optimization: \";\n350:             case \"Bit Manipulation\" -> \"Bitwise Operation: \";\n351:             case \"Trie\" -> \"Prefix Trie: \";\n352:             default -> \"Advanced DS: \";\n353:         };\n354: \n355:         String pattern = switch ((index % 6)) {\n356:             case 0 -> \"Optimal Partition\";\n357:             case 1 -> \"Range Query\";\n358:             case 2 -> \"Subsequence Transformation\";\n359:             case 3 -> \"Maximum Cost Path\";\n360:             case 4 -> \"Frequency Target\";\n361:             default -> \"K-Factor Evaluation\";\n362:         };\n363: \n364:         return prefix + pattern + \" Variant \" + index + \" (\" + diff.name().charAt(0) + diff.name().substring(1).toLowerCase() + \")\";\n365:     }\n366: \n367:     private String generateProblemDescription(String title, String category, Difficulty diff) {\n368:         return \"Given an input dataset representing standard competitive programming constraints for **\" + title + \"**,\\n\\n\" +\n369:                 \"Your task is to implement an optimal algorithm in **O(\" + getExpectedTimeComplexity(category, diff) + \")** time and **O(\" + getExpectedSpaceComplexity(category, diff) + \")** space.\\n\\n\" +\n370:                 \"### Task Details\\n\" +\n371:                 \"- Process the input stream adhering to all specified constraints.\\n\" +\n372:                 \"- Ensure execution efficiency and memory optimization for maximum duel scoring.\\n\" +\n373:                 \"- Handle edge cases including minimum boundary elements, duplicates, and extreme scale factors.\\n\";\n374:     }\n375: \n376:     private String generateConstraints(Difficulty diff) {\n377:         return switch (diff) {\n378:             case EASY -> \"- `1 <= nums.length <= 10^4`\\n- `-10^6 <= nums[i] <= 10^6`\\n- `Time limit: 2.0s`\\n- `Memory limit: 256MB`\";\n379:             case MEDIUM -> \"- `1 <= nums.length <= 10^5`\\n- `-10^9 <= nums[i] <= 10^9`\\n- `Time limit: 2.0s`\\n- `Memory limit: 256MB`\";\n380:             case HARD -> \"- `1 <= nums.length <= 2 * 10^5`\\n- `-10^9 <= nums[i] <= 10^9`\\n- `Queries count <= 10^5`\\n- `Time limit: 3.0s`\\n- `Memory limit: 256MB`\";\n381:         